**Supersedes:** [0002: duplicate reports share an evidenced cause](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).
Accepted decisions 0001 and 0002 remain unchanged as history.

## Context

Decision 0002 correctly separated causes, but its signature was the author's
GitHub handle. The course requires its issued ticket as the page signature.
This replacement records that provenance without editing an accepted decision.
The [incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) now uses the same issued
signature; its render-time desk reference follows from that exact value.

## Decision

Retain the cause-based rule from decision 0002. Merge only when the evidence
supports a shared cause and compatible affected product and path. Deduplicate
report IDs, resolve tenant locale and form version, inspect the channel, and
read the body for contradictions. Use `causeOf` and `sameCause` for the date
cases, not subject matching, browser locale, or intake's guessed tags.

Unknown tenants, unsupported cases, and timing anomalies stay visible for
investigation rather than being forced into a cause. Preserve report IDs and
ticket links when reclassifying. Continue routing supported cases while
engineering investigates uncertainty.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

Current triage points here rather than to the superseded records. This changes
the recorded provenance, not the cause counts or evidence limits. Publishing
and signing a review does not prove a production fix, and closing course
deliverables does not resolve the unexplained timing reports.

